# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 143-146 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 14 — CHAPTER 16, LEAN, 2026-09-23): "times" as pilgrimages, to see and be seen, the males and
# the minors, the face turned to you, the order of the feasts and "do not delay", not empty — the two houses' prices, each man's hand (143); the courts for all
# Israel, the one over all, city by city, tribe by tribe, the great and the lesser Sanhedrin, against their will, righteous judgment the appointment, the three
# prohibitions, the bribe even to acquit the innocent, justice justice — acquittal never reopened, guilt reopened, the good court, the land (144); the asherah
# and any tree beside the altar, the portico, the a fortiori from burning, even a house (145); the pillar loved by the fathers hated by the sons (146).
from ch16_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(143, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THREE TIMES" (16:16) — "TIMES" MEANS SEASONS. [ANOTHER WORD: "TIMES" MEANS PILGRIMAGES (FEET)], AND SO IT SAYS "THE FOOT SHALL TRAMPLE IT, THE FEET OF THE POOR, THE STEPS OF THE NEEDY" (ISAIAH 26:6). The head row of piska 143 ({SP_(143, 1, "אין", "פעמים", "אלא", "זמנים")} "times means only seasons"; {SP_(143, 1, "תרמסנה", "רגל", "רגלי", "עני", "פעמי", "דלים")} "the foot shall trample it, the feet of the poor, the steps of the needy"): 16:16\'s "times" and Exodus 23:14\'s "feet" (regalim) made one word by Isaiah\'s verse where foot, feet and steps stand together (never read ahead — the Prophets\' verse from its citation): the pilgrimage a walking. Fresh.')
srow(143, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"SHALL APPEAR" — AS HE COMES TO SEE, SO HE COMES TO BE SEEN. The row without a citation ({SP_(143, 2, "כדרך", "שבא", "לראות", "כך", "בא", "לראות")} "as he comes to see, so he comes to be seen"): the verb\'s two readings (the passive "be seen", the active "see") both kept — Chagigah 2a\'s segment (the blind in one eye) if a cell needs it. Fresh.')
srow(143, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR MALES" — TO EXCLUDE THE WOMEN. ({SP_(143, 3, "להוציא", "את", "הנשים")} "to exclude the women"): the appearance\'s subjects the males (138:7\'s joy both sexes). Fresh.')
srow(143, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"ALL YOUR MALES" — TO INCLUDE THE MINORS. ({SP_(143, 4, "להביא", "את", "הקטנים")} "to include the minors"): "all" widens to the minor able to go up — the next row\'s measure. Fresh.')
srow(143, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH CHAGIGAH 1:1): WHO IS A MINOR? WHOEVER CANNOT RIDE ON HIS FATHER\'S SHOULDERS TO GO UP FROM JERUSALEM TO THE TEMPLE MOUNT — THE HOUSE OF SHAMMAI, FROM "YOUR MALES"; THE HOUSE OF HILLEL: WHOEVER CANNOT HOLD HIS FATHER\'S HAND TO GO UP, FROM "THREE FEET" (EXODUS 23:14). ({SP_(143, 5, "לרכוב", "על", "כתפו", "של", "אביו")} "to ride on his father\'s shoulders"; {SP_(143, 5, "לאחוז", "בידו", "של", "אביו")} "to hold his father\'s hand"): THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW ITSELF — the minor\'s bound two ways from two verses\' words: the compile\'s age parameter with two arms (Chagigah 6a the segment). Fresh.')
srow(143, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'"THE FACE OF THE LORD YOUR GOD" — IF YOU DO ALL THAT IS SAID IN THE MATTER, I TURN FROM ALL MY AFFAIRS AND ATTEND ONLY TO YOU. ({SP_(143, 6, "פונה", "אני", "מכל", "עסקי")} "I turn from all My affairs"): the face\'s promise. Fresh.')
srow(143, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AT THE FEAST OF UNLEAVENED BREAD, THE FEAST OF WEEKS AND THE FEAST OF BOOTHS" — R. SIMEON SAYS: NO NEED TO SAY BOOTHS, THE VERSE\'S OWN SUBJECT; WHY WEEKS AND BOOTHS? IT TEACHES THAT ONE DOES NOT TRANSGRESS "DO NOT DELAY" UNTIL THE WHOLE YEAR\'S PILGRIMAGES HAVE PASSED. ({SP_(143, 7, "אין", "תלמוד", "לומר", "בחג", "הסכות")} "no need to say at the feast of booths"; {SP_(143, 7, "משם", "בל", "תאחר")} "under do not delay"): THE ORDER OF THE THREE NAMES READ AS A CLOCK — the vow\'s delay (23:22, ahead) measured in three feasts in order: the compile\'s delay window (Mishnah Rosh Hashanah 1:1 / 4a the segment); 2 Chronicles 8:13 the one other verse with the three names in this order (asserted, the run\'s case). Fresh.')
srow(143, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SHALL NOT APPEAR BEFORE THE LORD EMPTY" — OF ALMS; AND THE SAGES GAVE A MEASURE: THE HOUSE OF SHAMMAI, THE APPEARANCE TWO SILVER AND THE REJOICING A MAAH; THE HOUSE OF HILLEL, THE APPEARANCE A MAAH AND THE REJOICING TWO SILVER. ({SP_(143, 8, "מן", "הצדקה")} "of alms"; {SP_(143, 8, "הראיה", "מעה", "כסף", "ושמחה", "שתי", "כסף")} "the appearance a maah of silver and the rejoicing two silver"): THE MISHNAH IN THE HEBREW (Chagigah 1:2) — "empty" the one seat of the phrase (asserted); the two offerings\' floors a disputed pair: the compile\'s price parameters. Fresh.')
srow(143, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"EACH MAN AS HIS HAND GIVES" (16:17) — FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH CHAGIGAH 1:5): MANY MOUTHS AND FEW GOODS, MANY PEACE OFFERINGS AND FEW BURNT; FEW MOUTHS AND MANY GOODS, MANY BURNT AND FEW PEACE; BOTH FEW — THE MAAH AND THE TWO SILVER; BOTH MANY — "EACH MAN AS HIS HAND GIVES, AS THE BLESSING OF THE LORD". ({SP_(143, 9, "אוכלים", "מרבים", "ונכסים", "מועטים")} "many eaters and few goods"; {SP_(143, 9, "זה", "וזה", "מרבה")} "both many"): THE MISHNAH IN THE HEBREW A THIRD TIME IN THE PISKA — the gift scaled by mouths and means: a two-input parameter; 16:17 shares six tokens in order with 12:15\'s "as the blessing of the LORD your God which He has given you" (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(144, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"JUDGES AND OFFICERS" (16:18) — WHENCE THAT THEY APPOINT A COURT FOR ALL ISRAEL? "JUDGES … YOU SHALL SET FOR YOURSELF". AND OFFICERS FOR ALL ISRAEL? "OFFICERS YOU SHALL SET FOR YOURSELF". The head row of piska 144 ({SP_(144, 1, "שממנים", "בית", "דין", "לכל", "ישראל")} "that they appoint a court for all Israel"): THE COURT FOR ALL ISRAEL FROM "FOR YOURSELF" — the first tier; the two nouns two offices, each read alone (Mishnah Sanhedrin 1 the answer sheet): the compile\'s daemon THE COURTS, installed at this verse with three tiers. Fresh.')
srow(144, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH SAYS: WHENCE THAT THEY APPOINT ONE OVER THEM ALL? "YOU SHALL SET FOR YOURSELF", AND IT SAYS "AND THE LEVITE OFFICERS BEFORE YOU" (2 CHRONICLES 19:11). ({SP_(144, 2, "אחד", "על", "גבי", "כלם")} "one over them all"): the head of all courts — the Chronicler\'s verse (Jehoshaphat\'s courts) the run\'s case, never read ahead. Fresh.')
srow(144, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE A COURT FOR EACH CITY? "JUDGES … IN ALL YOUR GATES"; OFFICERS FOR EACH CITY? "AND OFFICERS … IN ALL YOUR GATES". ({SP_(144, 3, "בית", "דין", "לכל", "עיר", "ועיר")} "a court for each and every city"): THE SECOND TIER FROM "IN ALL YOUR GATES" — the book\'s four seats of the phrase (asserted): the courts\' seats the cities. Fresh.')
srow(144, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE A COURT FOR EACH TRIBE? "JUDGES … FOR YOUR TRIBES"; OFFICERS FOR EACH TRIBE? "AND OFFICERS … FOR YOUR TRIBES". RABBAN SIMEON BEN GAMALIEL SAYS: "FOR YOUR TRIBES, AND THEY SHALL JUDGE" — A COMMANDMENT ON EACH TRIBE TO JUDGE ITS OWN. ({SP_(144, 4, "בית", "דין", "לכל", "שבט", "ושבט")} "a court for each and every tribe"; {SP_(144, 4, "להיות", "דן", "את", "שבטו")} "to be judging its tribe"): THE THIRD TIER FROM "FOR YOUR TRIBES" — the tribe\'s court; the tape\'s population by tribe the seats\' data (Tosefta Sanhedrin 3:10). Fresh.')
srow(144, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN ALL YOUR GATES" — IT COMES TO COMPARE THE GREAT SANHEDRIN TO THE SMALL: AS THE GREAT JUDGES AND EXECUTES, SO THE SMALL JUDGES AND EXECUTES. ({SP_(144, 5, "להקיש", "סנהדרי", "גדולה", "לסנהדרי", "קטנה")} "to compare the great Sanhedrin to the small Sanhedrin"; {SP_(144, 5, "דנה", "והורגת")} "judges and executes"): THE CITY COURT\'S CAPITAL POWER by comparison with the great court (Mishnah Sanhedrin 1:1, 1:4 the exam — twenty-three and seventy-one): the compile\'s tiers carry the same verdict set; the English\'s note the row\'s thin attestation. Fresh.')
srow(144, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY SHALL JUDGE THE PEOPLE" — AGAINST THEIR WILL. ({SP_(144, 6, "בעל", "כרחם")} "against their will"): the court\'s jurisdiction compulsory — an effect on the people, not a service they ask. Fresh.')
srow(144, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"RIGHTEOUS JUDGMENT" — IS IT NOT ALREADY SAID "YOU SHALL NOT WREST JUDGMENT" (16:19)? WHAT THEN "RIGHTEOUS JUDGMENT"? THIS IS THE APPOINTMENT OF THE JUDGES. ({SP_(144, 7, "זה", "מנוי", "הדינים")} "this is the appointment of the judges"): 16:18\'s "righteous" moved from the verdict to the APPOINTMENT — a duty on the appointer; the next two rows read 16:19\'s prohibitions the same way. Fresh.')
srow(144, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT WREST JUDGMENT" (16:19) — THAT YOU NOT SAY: SO-AND-SO IS HANDSOME, SO-AND-SO IS MY KINSMAN. ({SP_(144, 8, "איש", "פלוני", "נאה", "איש", "פלוני", "קרובי")} "so-and-so is handsome, so-and-so is my kinsman"): the first prohibition read on the appointer (the seating of judges by looks or kin) — the three seats of the phrase in the Torah (Exodus 23:6, here, 24:17 — asserted). Fresh.')
srow(144, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT RESPECT PERSONS" — THAT YOU NOT SAY: SO-AND-SO IS POOR, SO-AND-SO IS RICH. ({SP_(144, 9, "איש", "פלוני", "עני", "איש", "פלוני", "עשיר")} "so-and-so is poor, so-and-so is rich"): the second prohibition — Leviticus 19:15\'s pair (the poor and the great) the kin (credited); the singular here against 1:17\'s plural (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(144, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL NOT TAKE A BRIBE" — NO NEED TO SAY TO ACQUIT THE GUILTY AND CONVICT THE INNOCENT, BUT EVEN TO ACQUIT THE INNOCENT AND CONVICT THE GUILTY. "FOR THE BRIBE BLINDS THE EYES OF THE WISE" — NO NEED TO SAY THE FOOLS\'; "AND PERVERTS THE WORDS OF THE RIGHTEOUS" — NO NEED TO SAY THE WICKED\'S. ANOTHER WORD: THEY CALL THE UNCLEAN CLEAN AND THE CLEAN UNCLEAN … THE FORBIDDEN PERMITTED. ANOTHER WORD: HE DOES NOT LEAVE THE WORLD UNTIL HE RULES RIGHTLY. ({SP_(144, 10, "אפלו", "לזכות", "את", "הזכי", "ולחיב", "את", "החיב")} "even to acquit the innocent and convict the guilty"; {SP_(144, 10, "ואין", "צריך", "לומר", "עיני", "טפשים")} "and no need to say the eyes of fools"): THE BRIBE\'S BAN ABSOLUTE — even for a true verdict (Ketubot 105a-b the segment); "THE WISE" read as the greater case of the fools (I1\'s shape in "no need to say", named without a code) — Exodus 23:8\'s "open-eyed" replaced by "wise" here (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(144, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND PERVERTS THE WORDS OF THE RIGHTEOUS" — HE DOES NOT LEAVE THE WORLD UNTIL HE KNOWS WHAT HE SAYS. ANOTHER WORD: "YOU SHALL NOT WREST JUDGMENT" — IN MONEY; "YOU SHALL NOT RESPECT PERSONS" — IN CAPITAL LAW. ANOTHER WORD: "YOU SHALL NOT RESPECT PERSONS" — IN HONOR: SEAT NOT THE LOWER ABOVE NOR THE HIGHER BELOW. ({SP_(144, 11, "לא", "תטה", "משפט", "בממון", "לא", "תכיר", "פנים", "בדין")} "you shall not wrest judgment — in money; you shall not respect persons — in law"; {SP_(144, 11, "הראוי", "למטה", "למעלה")} "the one fit for below, above"): the two prohibitions split by case type (money, capital) or by seating — the compile\'s two cells (Sanhedrin 32a the segment). Fresh.')
srow(144, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"JUSTICE YOU SHALL PURSUE" (16:20) — WHENCE THAT ONE WHO LEFT THE COURT ACQUITTED IS NOT BROUGHT BACK TO CONVICTION? THE TEACHING SAYS "JUSTICE, JUSTICE YOU SHALL PURSUE". ({SP_(144, 12, "יצא", "מבית", "דין", "זכי", "אין", "מחזירים", "אותו", "לחובה")} "one who left the court acquitted is not returned to conviction"): THE DOUBLED WORD READ AS TWO RULES — the one seat of "justice, justice" in the Bible (asserted): an acquittal final (Mishnah Sanhedrin 4:1 the exam): the compile\'s verdict effect irreversible in one direction. Fresh.')
srow(144, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'IF HE LEFT CONVICTED, WHENCE THAT THEY BRING HIM BACK TO ACQUITTAL? AS IT IS SAID "JUSTICE, JUSTICE YOU SHALL PURSUE". ({SP_(144, 13, "שמחזירים", "אותו", "לזכות")} "they return him to acquittal"): the other direction open — the two "justice" the two rules. Fresh.')
srow(144, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "JUSTICE, JUSTICE YOU SHALL PURSUE" — PURSUE A COURT WHOSE JUDGMENT IS GOOD, AFTER THE COURT OF RABBAN JOHANAN BEN ZAKKAI AND THE COURT OF R. ELIEZER. ({SP_(144, 14, "רדף", "אחר", "בית", "דין", "שדינו", "יפה")} "pursue after a court whose judgment is good"): the pursuit of the good court — the litigant\'s choice a second reading (Sanhedrin 32b the segment). Fresh.')
srow(144, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT YOU MAY LIVE AND INHERIT THE LAND" — IT TEACHES THAT THE APPOINTMENT OF JUDGES SUFFICES TO KEEP ISRAEL ALIVE, TO SETTLE THEM ON THEIR LAND, AND NOT TO FELL THEM BY THE SWORD. ({SP_(144, 15, "שמנוי", "הדינים", "כדי", "הוא", "להחיות", "את", "ישראל")} "that the appointment of the judges suffices to keep Israel alive"): THE COURTS\' EFFECT ON THE LAND — the receipt clause (one seat, asserted) tied to the appointment; the tape\'s land status the effect\'s ledger. Fresh.')
srow(145, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT PLANT FOR YOURSELF AN ASHERAH OF ANY TREE" (16:21) — IT TEACHES THAT WHOEVER PLANTS AN ASHERAH TRANSGRESSES A PROHIBITION. AND WHENCE THAT ONE WHO PLANTS A TREE ON THE TEMPLE MOUNT TRANSGRESSES? "ANY TREE BESIDE THE ALTAR OF THE LORD YOUR GOD". The head row of piska 145 ({SP_(145, 1, "שכל", "הנוטע", "אשרה", "עובר", "בלא", "תעשה")} "that whoever plants an asherah transgresses a prohibition"; {SP_(145, 1, "לנוטע", "אילן", "בהר", "הבית")} "one who plants a tree on the Temple Mount"): TWO PROHIBITIONS FROM ONE VERSE — the asherah anywhere, any tree beside the altar: the compile\'s two cells with two seats (everywhere; the Mount); the asherah bare here and at Exodus 34:13 (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(145, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER BEN JACOB SAYS: WHENCE THAT THEY MAKE NO WOODEN PORTICO IN THE COURT? "ANY TREE BESIDE THE ALTAR"; AND WHEN IT SAYS "WHICH YOU SHALL MAKE FOR YOURSELF" — TO INCLUDE A HIGH PLACE. ({SP_(145, 2, "שאין", "עושים", "אכסדרה", "בעזרה")} "that they make no portico in the court"; {SP_(145, 2, "לרבות", "במה")} "to include a high place"): "tree" read as WOOD (the English\'s note) — no wooden structure in the court; the high place\'s altar included in the eras when altars were permitted (chapter 12\'s table): Tamid 28b the segment. Fresh.')
srow(145, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT PLANT FOR YOURSELF AN ASHERAH" — THE TORAH SAID "AND THEIR ASHERAHS YOU SHALL BURN WITH FIRE" (12:3): AN A FORTIORI THAT HE NOT PLANT! WHENCE THAT HE NOT MAINTAIN ONE? "YOU SHALL NOT PLANT FOR YOURSELF" — IN ANY CASE. ({SP_(145, 3, "קל", "וחומר", "שלא", "יטע")} "an a fortiori that he not plant"; {SP_(145, 3, "ומנין", "שלא", "יקים")} "and whence that he not maintain"): I1 (checked) FROM 12:3\'s BURNING TO THE PLANTING — the verse then needed for MAINTAINING: the prohibition\'s object widened to keeping one standing (Avodah Zarah 48a the segment). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 12\'s sitting, deu_12_reeh).')
srow(145, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: EVEN A HOUSE, EVEN [A BOOTH]. The row without a citation, its end missing in the print ({SP_(145, 4, "אפלו", "בית", "אפלו")} "even a house, even"): the asherah\'s ban reaching a house and a booth made of it (the English\'s note supplies the last word). Fresh.')
srow(146, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL NOT SET UP FOR YOURSELF A PILLAR" (16:22) — I HAVE ONLY A PILLAR; WHENCE AN IDOL? IT IS A REASONING: IF THE PILLAR, LOVED BY THE FATHERS, IS HATED BY THE SONS, THE IDOL, HATED BY THE FATHERS — IS IT NOT REASON THAT IT BE HATED BY THE SONS? The one row of piska 146 ({SP_(146, 1, "שאהובה", "לאבות", "שנואה", "לבנים")} "that was loved by the fathers, hated by the sons"; {SP_(146, 1, "דין", "הוא", "שתהא", "שנואה", "לבנים")} "it is reason that it be hated by the sons"): I1 (checked) FROM THE PILLAR TO THE IDOL, BUILT ON THE TAPE\'S OWN HISTORY — Jacob\'s pillars (Genesis 28:18, 31:45, 35:14, 20 — the pillar\'s eleven Torah seats asserted) loved then, "which the LORD your God hates" now (the one seat of the phrase; 12:31\'s "which the LORD hates" its kin): a law whose reason is a CHANGE OF STATE across the tape — the compile\'s pillar cell with an era condition (the fathers\' era permitted, the sons\' banned). Fresh.')
